OpenLambda robot inference

The observation alignment, Lambda0 preprocessing, hand-target clamping,
signed action envelope and runtime attachment logic are adapted from the
lambda0-inference deployment workspace. This extraction removes model registry,
web console, task-specific configuration and automatic service deployment,
and uses the public lambda0 serve API for model loading and prediction.

The terminal runtime, normalized-STARK hand adapter and optional runtime header
are original OpenLambda integrations. The additional SONIC patch inserts minimal
integration hooks into the separately obtained public NVlabs/GR00T-WholeBodyControl
source, pinned to b042411fae38ee4d1af9aac82a37a1f8d14d6dd0. It does not redistribute
the SONIC controller binary, hardware SDKs or model weights.

The timestamped live camera adapter reuses OpenLambda's public robot-collection
clock calibration and MPEG-TS timing components. Collection provenance is covered
by data_collection/robot/NOTICE and the repository root NOTICE.

SONIC, hardware SDKs and model weights remain separately installed components
under their original licenses. Keep their upstream notices and license files
when installing or modifying those components; OpenLambda's license does not
relicense external code, model assets or SDKs.
